course: dictionary
lesson: 14785
title: Psychic: a word to think about carefully
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Psychic is a word people use when they talk about knowing things that no one can see or prove. A psychic is a person who says they can know the future, read minds or talk to the dead. «The woman at the fair said she was a psychic.» Here, a psychic means a person with those special claims.
explain: Psychic can also be an adjective, a describing word. «The film was full of psychic powers.» The word psychic tells us what kind of powers they were: powers of the mind, not ordinary powers. You can spot it because it describes a thing, like powers or a reading.
explain: Words about truth need care. «I'm not psychic!» means the speaker does not claim to know secret things. «Scientists have never proved that psychic powers are real.» This sentence does not say psychic powers are fake. It says nobody has shown they are real. Read the words around the word to see what the author is saying.
fact: A psychic is a person who says they can know the future, read minds or talk to the dead.
fact: Psychic is also an adjective: «psychic powers» means powers of the mind.
fact: «A psychic reading» means a session where a psychic says they tell you things about your life or future.
fact: Scientists have never proved that psychic powers are real.
fact: In lessons about tricks and truth, pupils learn that some people who claim to be psychic trick others into paying them money.
exercise: «The woman at the fair said she was a psychic.» What does psychic mean in this sentence? | A kind of fair game with prizes | A loud noise made by a crowd | A type of sweet food | *A person who says they can know the future or read minds
exercise: In «psychic powers», psychic describes the powers. What kind of word is psychic here? | A noun | *An adjective | A verb | An adverb
exercise: Mia says, «Scientists have never proved that psychic powers are real.» What does this sentence tell us? | *Nobody has yet shown that psychic powers are real | Psychic powers only appear in films | Scientists are psychic themselves | Psychic powers have been proved to exist
test: «The film's hero had psychic powers and could read everyone's thoughts.» What does psychic mean in this sentence? | Very fast on a bike | Able to hear very well | Covered in colourful paint | *Having powers of the mind, like knowing thoughts
test: Sam reads, «A psychic reading costs ten pounds.» What is a psychic reading? | *A session where a psychic claims to tell you things about your life | A reading lesson at school | A book about the history of the fair | A quiz about fast cars
exam: Ruby says, «I'm not psychic!» What does she mean? | She has lost her voice | She is a famous fortune teller | She can read minds very well | *She does not claim to know secret things or the future
